    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0305" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg205"/>

                <head>No. 134.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kasson to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 27, 1884.</date>
                        (Received November 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 53.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 278 and
                    to my No. 41, I beg herewith to inclose to you a copy of my note to the foreign
                    office requesting its mediation to convey the thanks of my Government to the
                    authorities for their action against the recruiting going on in Bavaria of
                    Mormon polygamists for transport to the United States.</p>
                <p>As any action of expulsion of Americans claiming converts in the name of religion
                    passes over dangerous roads, I beg your attention to the grounds upon which I
                    placed your approval of the proceedings in Bavaria.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN A. KASSON.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d134-a1.xml" xpointer="d134-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
